DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  uusseellooccaallee()  function  sets  the  current  locale  for the calling
       thread, and returns the thread’s previously current  locale.   After  a
       successful  call  to uusseellooccaallee(), any calls by this thread to functions
       that depend on the locale will operate as though the  locale  has  been
       set to _n_e_w_l_o_c.

       The _n_e_w_l_o_c argument can have one of the following values:

       A handle returned by a call to
              nneewwllooccaallee(3) or dduuppllooccaallee(3) The calling thread’s current locale
              is set to the specified locale.

       The special locale object handle
              LLCC__GGLLOOBBAALL__LLOOCCAALLEE  The  calling thread’s current locale is set to
              the global locale determined by sseettllooccaallee(3).

       _(_l_o_c_a_l_e___t_) _0
              The calling thread’s current locale is left unchanged  (and  the
              current locale is returned as the function result).

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On  success,  uusseellooccaallee() returns the locale handle that was set by the
       previous call to uusseellooccaallee() in this  thread,  or  LLCC__GGLLOOBBAALL__LLOOCCAALLEE  if
       there  was  no  such previous call.  On error, it returns _(_l_o_c_a_l_e___t_) _0,
       and sets _e_r_r_n_o to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
       EEIINNVVAALL _n_e_w_l_o_c does not refer to a valid locale object.

